---
globs: **/*.cjs, **/*.js, **/*.jsx, **/*.mjs, **/*.ts, **/*.tsx, **/*.vue
alwaysApply: false
---

Modules:
- Use ES modules with `import` and `export` by default; fall back to CommonJS `require()` only when required by the surrounding tool or config format
- Use named exports by default; reserve default exports for framework-required entry points (e.g. config files, Next.js pages, Nuxt plugins)

Async code:
- Prefer `async` functions and `await` over Promise `.then()` chains

Constants:
- Group related constants inside an object literal when they form a lookup table (e.g. error codes, messages, settings); keep standalone constants otherwise

Errors:
- Implement domain-specific error types (see core/clean-code) by extending the built-in `Error` class
